  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What happened (before 23b2ca7)",
      "items": [
        "Events go to the backends on the phone's thread: deliver() holds PhoneServer.lock while handle() and emit() run (wsserver.py 271–277, core.py 69–86).",
        "Link.send wrote with no time limit. A backend that is still connected but reads nothing (its PC asleep or gone from the Wi-Fi) fills its socket in a few photos; the next write blocks until TCP gives up, minutes later.",
        "Meanwhile the phone's later messages are not read, and take_over() waits for the same lock, so no other phone can join (wsserver.py 265–269). Impact: the whole edge stops for a flow that went away."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Fix and test",
      "items": [
        "Link sets SO_SNDTIMEO (SEND_TIMEOUT_S = 10) on its socket: a write without progress for 10 s fails, the link is marked closed and shut, so its reader ends and the backend leaves the list (wsserver.py 152–185). Reads still wait as long as they like.",
        "tests/test_adapters.py test_a_stuck_backend_is_dropped: a backend that never reads, six photo taps; all seven events are emitted, the stuck backend is gone, and a second phone takes over. Reproduced first with a script: 4 of 8 events, no takeover in 15 s."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Still true",
      "items": [
        "One slow backend still delays the phone by up to 10 s per event while it lasts; a queue per backend would remove that, at the cost of memory for photos. Open, by design for now."
      ]
    }
  ]
